pdate of a randomized trial</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>1999</year><volume>281</volume><fpage>1586</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10235147</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.281.17.1586</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Montgomery</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Krupa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooke</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patients' expectations for follow-up in breast cancer: a preliminary, questionnaire-based study</article-title><source>Breast</source><year>2008</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>347</fpage><lpage>352</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18455404</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.breast.2008.02.004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baildam</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Keeling</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bundred</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopwood</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nurse-led surgical follow up clinics for women treated for breast cancer &#x02013; a randomised controlled trial</article-title><source>Breast Cancer Res Treat</source><year>2004</year><volume>88</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>S136</fpage><lpage>S137</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Montgomery</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Krupa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooke</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alternative methods of follow up in breast cancer: a systematic review of the literature</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2007</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>1625</fpage><lpage>1632</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17486134</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.bjc.6603771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saphner</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tormey</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Annual hazard rates of recurrence for breast cancer after primary therapy</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1996</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>2738</fpage><lpage>2746</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8874335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Montgomery</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Krupa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jack</surname><given-names>WJL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerr</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kunkler</surname><given-names>IH</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixon</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changing pattern of the detection of loco-regional relapse in breast cancer: the Edinburgh experience</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2007</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>1802</fpage><lpage>1807</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17533401</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.bjc.6603815</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>